{
 "version": 1,
 "_comment": [
  "An ivy-clad stone arcade (spec 11.51). 24 'n'-profile ribs at a 1.75 m",
  "pitch; the gaps are what let the sun in, and the pitch is set against the",
  "FOLIAGE depth rather than the stone, or the canopy from adjacent ribs meets",
  "in the middle and seals them.",
  "",
  "Framed from OUTSIDE and well back, which is what the reference is: at that",
  "distance the green MASS registers and a leaf is fine texture, so the cards",
  "carry clumps rather than single leaves and are sized accordingly.",
  "",
  "Sun high and across, not low and down the axis. High because the target is",
  "a bright sunlit hedge, not a cave -- the earlier low-sun framing lit the",
  "outside and left the whole structure reading as a silhouette."
 ],
